 """Builds one DAG per pipeline config in configs/pipelines/*.yaml.
 
 Each config names its team (looked up in the platform registry for owners and
-retry defaults), a schedule (hour and day-of-week; the start minute is spread
-over the hour so the warehouse does not get every pipeline at :00) and a list
-of steps. Every step becomes a task that runs `run_step`.
+retry defaults), a tier (`critical` or `standard`), a schedule (hour and
+day-of-week; the start minute is spread over the hour so the warehouse does not
+get every pipeline at :00) and a list of steps. Every step becomes a task that
+runs `run_step` in the shared `warehouse` pool.
+
+Parse-time rules this file follows (the DAG processor re-parses it every few
+seconds and every worker parses it before running a task):
+
+* The registry is read once per parse with the libyaml loader, not once per DAG.
+* Everything that ends up in a DAG is deterministic: no clock, no salted
+  ``hash()``, no set iteration. The same configs always serialize to the same
+  DAGs, so there is no new DAG version unless a config changes.
+* Each config is validated as plain data, then built into a DAG that is not
+  registered until it is known to be good. A broken config logs an error that
+  names the file and is skipped; every other pipeline still loads.
+* When a worker parses the file for one task, only that task's DAG is built.
 """
 
